Q: Can&#39;t change color of included theme A: <p>Okay, your configuration works by default, but you did not set either a light or dark theme as the default. You could only override DaisyUI's default colors by using a completely new template, but in that case you would be forced to redeclare every color; for example, by using your own theme generator:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://daisyui.com/theme-generator" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://daisyui.com/theme-generator</a></li>
<li><a href="https://play.tailwindcss.com/YgMzhYw30x?file=css" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://play.tailwindcss.com/YgMzhYw30x?file=css</a></li>
</ul>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>@import &quot;tailwindcss&quot;;

@plugin &quot;daisyui&quot; {
  themes: defaultTheme --default, light, dark;
}

/*  default without data-theme */
@plugin &quot;daisyui/theme&quot; {
  name: &quot;defaultTheme&quot;;
  default: true;
  --color-secondary: #0088ff;
  --color-secondary-content: #07345b;
}

/*  data-theme=&quot;dark&quot; */
@plugin &quot;daisyui/theme&quot; {
  name: &quot;dark&quot;;
  default: false;
  --color-secondary: #0a0a0a;
  --color-secondary-content: #ddd;
}

/*  data-theme=&quot;light&quot; */
@plugin &quot;daisyui/theme&quot; {
  name: &quot;light&quot;;
  default: false;
  --color-secondary: #fff;
  --color-secondary-content: #333;
}
</code></pre>
<p>To avoid having to do this in such a poor way, you can override the colors in the no data-theme state at a much stronger layer, like this:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://play.tailwindcss.com/mK0LzcK4RO?file=css" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://play.tailwindcss.com/mK0LzcK4RO?file=css</a></li>
</ul>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>@import &quot;tailwindcss&quot;;
@plugin &quot;daisyui&quot;;

/*  default without data-theme */
@layer daisyui {
  :root, :host {
    --color-secondary: #0088ff;
    --color-secondary-content: #07345b;
  }
}

/*  data-theme=&quot;dark&quot; */
@plugin &quot;daisyui/theme&quot; {
  name: &quot;dark&quot;;
  default: false;
  --color-secondary: #0a0a0a;
  --color-secondary-content: #ddd;
}

/*  data-theme=&quot;light&quot; */
@plugin &quot;daisyui/theme&quot; {
  name: &quot;light&quot;;
  default: false;
  --color-secondary: #fff;
  --color-secondary-content: #333;
}
</code></pre>
